    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Followers of Tenrikyo believe that God of Origin, God in Truth, known as Tenri-O-no-Mikoto and Oyagami-sama, &quot;God the Parent&quot;, was revealed in 1838 through Nakayama Miki, whom they call Oyasama and regard as the Shrine of God.</li><li>Tenrikyo's worldly aim is the Joyous Life, cultivated through acts of charity and mindfulness called hinokishin, which sweep away the &quot;mental dusts&quot; of the mind, among them miserliness, covetousness and arrogance.</li><li>The ultimate spiritual aim is the construction of the Kanrodai at the Jiba and the correct performance of the Kagura ritual around it, which followers believe will bring about the salvation of all human beings.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Tenrikyo teaches that the human body is a thing lent by God and borrowed by the person, kashimono-karimono; only the mind is held to be one's own, so followers commonly accept that Tenri-O-no-Mikoto is not omnipotent.</p></aside>
    </section>

